*.log

# LEHAR Phase 2: alert-engine OPS event breadcrumbs (runtime state written
# by the training pipeline and the rollback endpoint — see
# app/services/alerts/ops_events.py).
ops_events.jsonl

# LEHAR Phase 2.5: the downloaded flood history the lead-time model trains on
# (scripts/data/fetch_flood_history.py). ~7MB of third-party Open-Meteo/GloFAS
# data that is re-downloadable at any time and is NOT this project's to
# redistribute in bulk. The _manifest.json beside it IS committed (see the
# negation below): it records exactly which districts were fetched, over which
# date range, with how many gaps — so the provenance of a trained model
# survives in git even though the bytes do not. See docs/FLOOD_DL.md.
data/flood_history/*
!data/flood_history/_manifest.json
